ttps://cdn.dental-tribune.com/dti/0001/3d549181/cmVzaXplKHc9MjY0MDtoPTE0ODYpOnNoYXJwZW4obGV2ZWw9MCk6b3V0cHV0KGZvcm1hdD1qcGVnKQ/up/dt/2026/11/exocad-announces-DentalCAD-3.3-Chemnitz-service-release-2_3.jpg 2640w\" type=\"image/jpeg\"><img src=\"https://cdn.dental-tribune.com/dti/0001/3d549181/cmVzaXplKHc9MjY0MDtoPTE0ODYpOnNoYXJwZW4obGV2ZWw9MCk6b3V0cHV0KGZvcm1hdD1qcGVnKQ/up/dt/2026/11/exocad-announces-DentalCAD-3.3-Chemnitz-service-release-2_3.jpg\" alt=\"The service release also introduces artificial intelligence-powered margin line detection, which automatically identifies and traces the crown preparation margin from the 3D digital scan.\" loading=\"lazy\">\n\t</picture><p>The service release also introduces artificial intelligence-powered margin line detection, which automatically identifies and traces the crown preparation margin from the 3D digital scan.</p>\n\t<p>Beyond AI, DentalCAD 3.3 Chemnitz service release 2 introduces quality and workflow improvements, including enhancements to implant detection, easier integration with 3D printer CAM software and improved webview export. DentalCAD 3.3 Chemnitz service release 2 uses Microsoft .NET 10 to ensure continued security support for the underlying framework. Exocad therefore recommends that DentalCAD 3.3 Chemnitz users install the update. Further information about the release is available at <a href=\"https://exocad.com/dentalcad-chemnitz\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">exocad.com/dentalcad-chemnitz</a>.</p>","kind":"full"}